# The working tree this repository lives in also holds coursework, recordings and
# build output that must never be published. The rules below are deny-by-default
# for whole categories; anything that genuinely belongs in the repo and collides
# with a rule is un-ignored explicitly, so adding a file is always a deliberate
# act rather than a side effect of leaving it in a folder.

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ── Tooling / IDE / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Runtime artifacts: real captured traffic and real classifications ────────
# An alert database is a log of actual network activity on the machine that ran
# it, and a capture carries payloads (this project's own test captures include
# /etc/passwd dumps and SSH sessions). Neither is publishable.
*.db
*.db.demo-backup
*.pcap
*.pcapng
live_threat_logs.csv
temp_raw.csv
retrain_state.json
launcher.log

# Evidence captures auto-saved by the dashboard — named after real remote IPs.
# Matched by directory name rather than by full path: the dashboard exists twice
# (Aalok/Dashboard is canonical, APP/Dashboard is the patched desktop copy) and a
# path-anchored rule silently covers only one of them.
*/Dashboard/evidence/

# ── Credentials and operator-specific config ─────────────────────────────────
# Only the .example templates are published; see SECURITY.md.
notifier_config.json
baseline.txt

# ── Training data and model snapshots ────────────────────────────────────────
# Large, regenerable, and derived from real captures. The one exception is
# ai_ready_advanced_flows.csv, un-ignored below: reproduce_spec_metrics.py needs
# it, and its Source IP column has been pseudonymised.
#
# Matched by name, not by path, for the same reason as the evidence rule above:
# both Dashboard copies carry these files, so anchoring to Aalok/Dashboard left
# the APP/Dashboard copies of the real training data one `git add` from being
# published.
master_behavioral_dataset.csv
master_advanced_dataset.csv
model_versions/
Bulk PCAPS/
Temp_CSVs/
archive*/
*.preanon-backup

# Pre-redaction copies of published documents. These hold exactly the network
# identity that was scrubbed out of the released versions, so they must never be
# staged — least of all by a reflexive `git add -A`.
*.preredact-backup

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
build/
build_test/
dist/
dist_test/
installer/output/
*.spec.bak
Hybrid IDS/

# Distribution bundles — published as GitHub Release assets, not as repo files.
# The .exe alone is ~380 MB, well past GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit.
HybridIDS-Code-Share/
HybridIDS-.exe-Share/
*.zip
*.exe

# ── Coursework, personal and internal project material ───────────────────────
# None of this belongs in a public code repository.
Aalok/Weeks/
Aalok/Final Report and Slides/
Backup/
claude memory file/
# The bundle handed in through Teams, plus the link notes that go with it. The
# institutional submission is the channel for restricted material; none of it
# belongs in the public mirror.
Submission Made In Teams/
*.mp4
*.pptx
*.docx
*.pdf
CLAUDE.md
changes.txt
mp delivirable.txt
HOW TO USE.txt
WEEKLY_JOURNALS*.md
Major_Project_Direction*
Teaching Plan*
image.png
image (*).png

# ── Un-ignored: shipped artifacts that collide with the rules above ──────────
# Trained models the app loads at runtime. Without these a fresh clone starts
# with no classifier and silently falls back to the K-Means model. Listed for
# both dashboard copies — APP/Dashboard is what PyInstaller bundles into the exe,
# so a clone missing those models cannot build the desktop app.
!Aalok/Dashboard/rf_model.pkl
!Aalok/Dashboard/rf_scaler.pkl
!Aalok/Dashboard/advanced_data_scaler.pkl
!Aalok/Dashboard/advanced_kmeans_model.pkl
!Aalok/Dashboard/lstm_model.pt
!APP/Dashboard/rf_model.pkl
!APP/Dashboard/rf_scaler.pkl
!APP/Dashboard/advanced_data_scaler.pkl
!APP/Dashboard/advanced_kmeans_model.pkl
!APP/Dashboard/lstm_model.pt
!Rui Yang/models/*.pkl

# Evidence behind the published metrics.
!Aalok/Dashboard/ai_ready_advanced_flows.csv
!APP/Dashboard/ai_ready_advanced_flows.csv
!Aalok/TEST_RESULTS.md
